  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the probability difference and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome (Lottery A). However, the individual acknowledges the small probability difference but explicitly shifts focus to the size of the loss, preferring the smaller monetary loss (Lottery B) despite its lower probability of the favorable outcome. The individual does not use the higher probability of the favorable outcome as a guiding principle; instead, they dismiss the probability difference as negligible and base their decision on outcome magnitude. Therefore, the reasoning process contradicts the decision reason, which prioritizes probability differences. The individual’s justification does not align with the rule of the decision reason.",
