  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes comparing probabilities between lotteries and prefers the one with a higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this context, avoiding a loss (i.e., getting 0 Euros) is the most favorable outcome possible, and Lottery A has a 75% chance of this versus 50% for Lottery B. The individual explicitly compares the probability of losing money (i.e., not achieving the favorable outcome) and gives decisive weight to the lower probability of loss in A. Their deliberation aligns with evaluating the differences in probabilities and preferring the option with a higher chance of a favorable (non-loss) outcome. The information considered (probability of loss) and the justification (favoring lower probability of loss despite larger potential loss) match the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
